# Shell scripts and buildspecs must reach CodeBuild with LF endings.
#
# The working tree is Windows and git converts to CRLF on checkout, which is
# fine locally — bash on Windows tolerates it. CodeBuild runs Linux, where a
# script stored with CRLF fails on its first line with a message that names a
# carriage return nobody wrote:
#
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# `eol=lf` pins what is STORED, so the conversion can only ever go one way.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf

# Everything else follows the platform default.
*           text=auto

# Binary, so git never rewrites bytes inside them.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.webp      binary
*.pptx      binary
*.zip       binary
